messages.content:
Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: bfd/coffgen.c
Line: 346
Function: coff_real_object_p
Bug type: integer-overflow
CWE: CWE-190
Explanation: readsize is computed as (bfd_size_type) nscns * scnhsz without overflow checking. On 32-bit builds this multiplication can wrap, causing a too-small allocation in _bfd_alloc_and_read. The subsequent loop (lines 358-366) iterates i from 0 to nscns-1 and accesses external_sections + i * scnhsz, which will read past the allocated buffer, leading to an out-of-bounds read.

Source context:
```c
